# needs: task-host fixtures (a turn-task binding and a task status with an interaction, written by the shared task writers); see ../INTEGRATION.md
# A permission prompt, answered: Allow posts once, and the task goes on.
clock data record auth.state: auth state => 200 {"loggedIn":true}
clock data record submit: http POST /api/chat/submit/v2alpha1 => 202 {"turn":"turn-1","conversation":"conv-1"}
clock data record events: http GET /api/chat/events/v2alpha1?id=turn-1&after=0 => part {"seq":1,"kind":"permission","interaction":"ask-1","tool":"shell","input":"git push"}
clock data record allow: http POST /api/chat/permission/v2alpha1 => 200 {"interaction":"ask-1","answer":"allow"}
clock data record events: http GET /api/chat/events/v2alpha1?id=turn-1&after=0 => 200 {"seq":2,"kind":"state","state":"completed"}
clock data release auth.state
tap chat.composer
type chat.composer Push the fix
tap chat.composer.send
clock +16
clock data release submit
clock data release events
tree
tap task.permission.allow
tap task.permission.allow
clock data
clock data release allow
clock data release events
state task.state
